1
00:00:00,430 --> 00:00:03,160
AI coding agents can work without you watching.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,230
So why are we still tied to a desk?

3
00:00:06,410 --> 00:00:09,590
Picture this. In T3 Code, I start three agents.

4
00:00:09,990 --> 00:00:12,580
One builds, one tests, and one reviews.

5
00:00:14,290 --> 00:00:15,440
Then I walk away.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,800
With Even G2, I'd see which agent needs me,

7
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:20,330
right in my field of view.

8
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:23,300
Tests are done. What's next?

9
00:00:23,950 --> 00:00:27,370
A tap on the R1 ring could select “Run final checks.”

10
00:00:28,270 --> 00:00:29,840
The agent takes it from there.

11
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:34,650
No laptop. No phone. Just the update I need,

12
00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:36,780
when I need it.

13
00:00:37,650 --> 00:00:39,180
The rest of the day is mine.

14
00:00:41,490 --> 00:00:44,420
Your agents keep working. Your world keeps moving.

15
00:00:45,590 --> 00:00:48,900
That's the experience I want to build for Even Realities.
